[36m(TaskRunner pid=119614)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 504\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of finding the maximum value of a linear combination of sine and cosine functions. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -504\), so the maximum value is:
